A||||6||burdell1||Exhaust Manifolds
Z||000000||burdell1||04-07-99||10:54 PM||||I am having a problem with my exhaust manifolds leaking.  I got the problem fixed, but one of the bolts on the front manifold was broken off.  Does anyone out there know what the easiest way to repair this?  Can a person take out the interior (behind the seats) to get at it better?  Help! my mechanic said it would be a $500 job!<br>
Z||000001||theogre||04-08-99||02:45 PM||||there are only ugly, and very ugly, ways to get to that area. The mechanic has good reason to charge alot. This job could take hours.<p>I think even if you take out the upolstry, that you will also need to cut a whole into the firwall. I haven't had the upolstry out yet, I took a quick look at mine, looks like a real nightmare to get out.
Z||000002||burdell1||04-11-99||03:48 PM||||Doesn't anyone out there know of an easy way to fix a broken off bolt on the front exhaust manifold? Any help at all would be greatly appreciated!<br>
Z||000003||theogre||04-11-99||10:32 PM||||Sorry guy. There are no easy ways if you can't get hold of it.<p>You have to drill it, and use an extractor. Or you have to drill it over size, rethread, and use the next bigger bolt. This second method usually requires drilling out the manifold hole to clear the new bolt size.<p>getting at the thing to drill it is just as ugly. you either come thru the fire wall, or move the engine, or get real lucky and find a gear head 90degree drill. Even with the gear head, you'll likely need to cut down a bit to get in there.<p>once you get this fixed.... don't foget to put anti sieze on the bolts before you reassemble.
Z||000004||FieroMike||04-12-99||11:17 AM||||Burdell,<br>There is a way!  Undo the dogbone on top and the engine mount on the rear-left of the engine.  Put a ratchet-strap on the engine puller mount (by the intake) and the rear deck-lid latch (where it closes) ratchet the strap, this will pull the engine away from the firewall.  I did this to check my manifold for leaks and change the plugs and there was a least a foot and a half of space between the manifold and firewall.  This should give you enough room to drill it out. Good luck.
Z||000005||theogre||04-12-99||12:39 PM||||that's a good idea. and if you can find a right angle drill you get plenty of room, and don't need a short bit. You probably can do it with the deck lid on even.<p>just rememeber to take your time, drill straght, and don't go to deep.
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||04-12-99||11:48 PM||||Thanks Mike.<p>I wanted to get a set of headers for my 6 but didn`t know how to get back there, will that work?   Coast Fiero has a nice set. Has anyone installed a set?<p>
